infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  root
    label Three deadlock shapes, three fixes
    children
      - label A: lock-order inversion
        children
          - label Cause: two paths lock the same pair in opposite order
          - label Fix: one global lock order; intrinsic-key for dynamic pairs
      - label B: blocking op under a mutex
        children
          - label Cause: channel send, I/O, RPC or Wait while holding the lock
          - label Fix: copy under the lock, release, then send
      - label C: WaitGroup.Add races Wait
        children
          - label Cause: Add inside the child; Wait can see 0 and return early
          - label Fix: Add before go; pass by pointer; -race flags it
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
